[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309919687","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3309919687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3309919687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FSV3H","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T22:38:42Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T22:38:42Z","body":"When are recursive calls expected? Isn't the function effectively a leaf? (i.e. no non-leaf functions are called, which would risk recursive calls).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309919687/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309940406","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3309940406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3309940406,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FSa62","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T22:52:38Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T23:02:12Z","body":"> When are recursive calls expected? Isn't the function effectively a leaf? (i.e. no non-leaf functions are called, which would risk recursive calls).\r\n\r\nAll `_update_children_cache()` calls only runs inside methods that are thread guarded but i have seen some exceptions that can trigger this error.\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nString Node::_get_tree_string_pretty(const String &p_prefix, bool p_last) {\r\n\tString new_prefix = p_last ? String::utf8(\" ┖╴\") : String::utf8(\" ┠╴\");\r\n\t_update_children_cache();\r\n```\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nString Node::_get_tree_string(const Node *p_node) {\r\n\t_update_children_cache();\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd `SceneTreeFTI::_update_dirty_nodes`\r\n\r\nThis can result in concurrent calls since we set `data.children_cache_dirty = false` at the end of `Node::_update_children_cache_impl` which means any `_update_children_cache` from another thread can still see the cache as dirty while we are still updating it.\r\n\r\nI'd like to know if we can apply a better fix, currently i have added this to see when it happens (if it's possible).\r\n\r\nEdit: It looks like i was referring to the possibility of concurrent calls and not recursive calls.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309940406/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309981637","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3309981637","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3309981637,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FSk_F","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T23:18:33Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T23:18:33Z","body":"I was able to reproduce a concurrent call with this script.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends Control\r\n\r\nvar t : Thread\r\nvar node: Node = Node.new()\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n\tfor i in range(50000):\r\n\t\tnode.add_child(Node.new())\r\n\tt = Thread.new()\r\n\tt.start(_thread_func)\r\n\tnode.get_children(true)\r\n\tawait get_tree().process_frame\r\n\tvar tree = t.wait_to_finish()\r\n\tprint(tree)\r\n\tnode.queue_free()\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _thread_func() -> String:\r\n\tvar tree: String\r\n\tfor i in 10:\r\n\t\ttree = node.get_tree_string_pretty()\r\n\treturn tree\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1771\" height=\"639\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e7f2935-0073-4f09-b269-b6f4ca97cc6e\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309981637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309990475","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3309990475","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3309990475,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FSnJL","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T23:23:56Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T23:24:34Z","body":"Ah, right. That's not a recursive call though, that would be a concurrent call.\r\nI think the appropriate fix is to add thread guards to the tree string functions. Logging incorrect concurrent behavior doesn't really help solve the problem.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309990475/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310049568","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3310049568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3310049568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FS1kg","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T00:04:54Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T00:04:54Z","body":"> Ah, right. That's not a recursive call though, that would be a concurrent call. I think the appropriate fix is to add thread guards to the tree string functions. Logging incorrect concurrent behavior doesn't really help solve the problem.\r\n\r\nThanks for correcting me, I will be testing it again, but without the guard its hard to tell if it may happen again, can we keep it only for debug builds and instead of reporting an error we crash instead?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310049568/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310079457","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3310079457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3310079457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FS83h","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T00:22:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T00:23:20Z","body":"With current changes it's still happening, any ideas how to prevent it using the same script above ?\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1771\" height=\"1073\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2792cae-5b71-4f83-b432-2750cd166df5\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310079457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310111142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3310111142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3310111142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FTEmm","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T00:43:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T00:43:59Z","body":"Ok I think it's fixed now, I will do more tests later to make sure no method can invalidate the cache.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"884\" height=\"327\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95bfd418-a451-4c73-a0f6-8083a42a1c1c\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310111142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310123159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3310123159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3310123159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FTHiX","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T00:53:25Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T00:53:25Z","body":"OKAY! it appears that all of them can invalidate the cache if the node is outside the tree!\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends Control\r\n\r\nvar t : Thread\r\nvar node: Node = Node.new()\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n\tfor i in range(50000):\r\n\t\tnode.add_child(Node.new())\r\n\tt = Thread.new()\r\n\tt.start(_thread_func)\r\n\tnode.get_children(true)\r\n\tawait get_tree().process_frame\r\n\tvar arr: Array[Node] = t.wait_to_finish()\r\n\t#print(tree)\r\n\tnode.queue_free()\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _thread_func() -> Array[Node]:\r\n\tvar arr: Array[Node]\r\n\tfor i in 10:\r\n\t\tarr = node.get_children(true)\r\n\treturn arr\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsing `get_children()` from a thread invalidates the cache if the node is outside the tree, and nearly all the other methods that are using `_update_children_cache` can trigger a concurrent call.\r\n\r\nMost of them uses `data.tree && !Thread::is_main_thread()` which will not work when the node is outside the tree.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310123159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312675944","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3312675944","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3312675944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fc2xo","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T15:36:44Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T15:36:44Z","body":"I’m not sure what regressions these changes could introduce for Godot projects. If any of them cause threading-related regressions, I wouldn’t be able to fix them, and I don’t want this PR to become the source of such issues.\r\n\r\nMy original intent was only to add the `data.is_updating` variable and print an error, without touching other logic. Would it make sense to revert the other changes and only keep the additional code wrapped inside `#ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED`?\r\n\r\nAlso, I’d prefer to keep the cache guard in all builds, but only print the error in debug builds. This will be especially useful after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110650, since it can help detect cases where a child is added to the cache during an update (which would also indicate a bug).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312675944/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312699591","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110675#issuecomment-3312699591","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110675","id":3312699591,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fc8jH","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T15:44:35Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T15:48:44Z","body":"Also check https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110650#pullrequestreview-3239934774, This issue (adding children directly to cache while it's updating) can be avoided by using the new `data.updating_cache` from this PR.\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nif (!data.children_cache_dirty && can_push_back && !data.updating_cache) {\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312699591/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]